DESCRIPTION Multi-tool band, coordinate Helm health + pod readiness + k8sgpt diagnosis into a root cause; 'nothing failing' acceptable when true.

DEFINE CONST QUESTION AS "Which Helm releases are currently in a Failed or Pending state, what
  underlying pods are not Ready, and what does k8sgpt diagnose as the root cause?"
DEFINE CONST MAX_DURATION AS 600 seconds

ASSERT(POST to discussion endpoint returns 200 with conversationId)
ASSERT(SSE stream emits "thread_found" event within 30 seconds)
ASSERT(discussion completes with "done" event within MAX_DURATION)

# Multi-tool: multiple specialists typically engage (k8s-helm + k8s-workloads or k8sgpt);
# gate on at least 1 agree so a correct coordinator-led synthesis is not gated to 0.
ASSERT(at least 1 specialist contributes with signal=agree)
ASSERT(coordinator produces synthesis)
ASSERT(synthesis is non-empty)

# Synthesis should reference both Helm and pod concepts
ASSERT(synthesis CONTAINS "Helm" AND "pod")

# Reference-grounded quality, deferred LLM judge (FitnessCrew) scores the
# synthesis 0.0-1.0 against this ground truth from cluster-ground-truth-baseline.md.
ASSERT(DEFER synthesis REFLECTS "Combines Helm release health, pod readiness, and a k8sgpt diagnosis to identify what (if anything) is failing and the root cause. The correct answer is what the live cluster shows at the time of the question: it enumerates the real Helm releases and reports any in a Failed or Pending state, lists the pods that are not Ready by namespace and name with their live reason (including pods Pending on a cordoned or NotReady node), and gives the k8sgpt diagnosis or says what it found, tying the root cause to the live evidence. When no release is Failed or Pending and no pod is unhealthy, the correct answer is that nothing is currently failing, grounded in actually enumerating the releases. Asserting that helm returned empty or that there are no Helm releases contradicts reality. A failure, pod, release or cause that the live data does not show is fabrication, and a real failure that the live data shows but the answer leaves out is a miss.")
